text: lay out a text at its own width on one line on macOS

On macOS, a single-line text that gets exactly its measured width can
still end in "…" (and a wrapping one drop its last word to a second line),
as "M4B（含章节）" and "标题(可选)" do. Two causes:

1. Core Text spaces some characters apart by context, as a bracket next to
   a letter of another script (macOS 26.7: 1/8 to 1/5 em). Within a run it
   widens a glyph's advance; between runs of two fonts (SF / PingFang) it
   only moves the glyphs of the next run. Line.Width sums advances, so it
   came out short of Core Text's typographic width, and
   CTTypesetterSuggestLineBreak at that width broke the line early.
   coreText.line now folds such gaps into the advance of the glyph before
   them (foldRunGaps).
2. CTTypesetterSuggestLineBreak forgives a width 0.0002 short of the
   line's at most. A float32 sum of a long line's float32 advances loses
   more (2e-4 at 570 DIPs), so long lines broke early too. line() now sums
   in float64, and coreText.shape breaks at width * (1 + 1e-6).

TestOwnWidthFits lays out each text at its own width and checks it keeps
to one line and the glyphs stay within the width.
